hexagon: the GDN state and conv fusions with the rollback slots of a draft

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h           the two matchers: K > 1, the slot span, the alias guard
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp          the emit of the two fused ops, the spanning dummy tensor
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gated-delta-net-ops.c the shape guard of the fused state step
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c        the write of the K slots of the conv state

The problem

Speculative decoding asks the recurrent layers to keep the last K states, thus a rejected draft rolls
back without a copy: the app sets n_rs_seq = 4, and the graph then carries K = 4. The two fused ops of
the patches before this one accept K = 1 only, thus every speculative decode ran the unfused chain: the
state half costs about 5.5 ms of a token and the conv half about 0.2 ms, over 18 layers.

The state chain

The op writes the attention row and the new state. With K > 1 the output of GATED_DELTA_NET is
[S_v * H, 1 + K * S_v], and the CPU reference writes the state of the token into the snapshot slot
n_tokens - 1 - t, thus slot 0 holds the newest state. At one token only slot 0 is written, and the
matcher accepts the chain when the shape agrees with 1 + K * S_v. The DSP op takes K from op_params[0]
and validates the same shape.

The conv chain

At one token the graph writes the same pre-token state into each of the K slots, as K separate CPY
nodes of the same source. The matcher collects them, sorts them by the address of their destination,
and checks that slot g copies the column max(0, n_tokens - g) of the CONCAT and that the slots are
evenly strided. The K destinations are contiguous rows of the conv cache, thus the fused op takes one
synthetic tensor that spans them, with n_slots rows and the slot stride, and the DSP writes the same
row to each slot. The span is an input and an output of the op: the backend marks the output tensors
dirty, and the limit is 4 outputs and 10 inputs.

The alias guard

The fused op stands at the first CPY of the chain, which is up to 18 nodes before the SILU whose
output it writes. The graph allocator can give that output the bytes of a tensor that died earlier,
and the projection that the op reads is such a tensor. A measurement with ggml_gallocr over one layer
produced exactly that overlap. The kernel loads a channel before it stores the same channel, thus the
result is correct today, but the property is not part of the contract of the op. The matcher now
refuses a chain whose projection and output share bytes.

A batch of tokens still refuses both fusions: the chunked delta rule of patch 0005 covers the prefill
and it keeps the final state only.

State of the verification

The matchers, the slot mapping, the completeness of the member lists and the addresses of the span
were checked on the host against the real graph allocator and the CPU reference (2026-09-19): the
slot stride of the 2B is 73728 bytes, the span covers 294912 bytes and no foreign byte, the attention
row and the snapshot slot 0 of K = 4 equal those of K = 1 exactly, and no member runs twice or is
skipped. The kernels themselves are not yet measured on the device.
